es across network configurations, web exposures, application integrations, data stores, and automation scripts. Risk assessment will define a quarantine window, and the Change Request (RFC) will \n<truncated 187 bytes>\n notifications to relevant teams. Next step requires updating a central inventory with the decommissioning status and associated metadata. Subsequently, supervision systems must be configured to prevent alerts and escalations. Finally, validate the backup and data retention plan, including full backups before shutdown.\n\n\nBackup configuration files and data to a secure storage location, adhering to the validated retention policy and verifying data integrity via checksums and read tests. Technical shutdown involves stopping services, OS shutdown, removing the server from automated inventories, and disabling SSH access, followed by a quarantine period. Security team will disable firewall rules associated with the equipment's IP, keeping the rules disabled during the quarantine period.\n\n\nFollowing the quarantine period, decommissioning involves definitive equipment removal: virtual machines are deleted, physical servers are dismantled and disks securely erased, and network/storage resources are cleaned up (SAN LUNs, NFS exports, virtual interfaces). DNS entries are removed and the central inventory system is updated, freeing the IP address.\n\nNext, firewall rules are permanently deleted, removing orphaned address objects, groups, and cleaning NAT tables and external publication rules. The final step is to create a technical decommissioning report.\n\n\nThe decommissioning report will include key information such as the decommissioning and definitive removal dates, backup references, and recovered disk/memory space. The Change Advisory Board (CAB) ticket will be closed with a \"Closed - Successful\" status, and the initiating ticket will be closed with final notification sent.\n\nA comprehensive operational checklist in an interactive table will be included, alongside a detailed rollback plan for issues identified during the quarantine period. A decommissioning report template will be developed. The ability to render markdown elements (tables, checkboxes, callout blocks, and code) within Outline documents must be verified.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport requests\\n\\nTOKEN = 'eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjY2ZDAwY2I0LWEzY2YtNDIyYS1hMjQ5LWVkMzA2NzEwZDdjZiIsImV4cGlyZXNBdCI6IjIwMjYtMTItMDhUMTA6NDU6MjcuNzkzWiIsInR5cGUiOiJzZXNzaW9uIiwic2VydmljZSI6ImF6dXJlIiwiaWF0IjoxNzg4ODY0MzI3fQ.tQTTmIeOP_H2i-10PROwjV-c_snixZFU5pG6CpKXXCk'\\nBASE_URL = 'https://wiki.corp.intranet.local'\\n\\npayload = {\\n    'title': 'Test Doc Verification',\\n    'text': '# Test\\\\nThis is a test doc',\\n    'collectionId': 'bda1a3da-cc3d-4c5d-92d1-d831dfbe2eae',\\n    'parentDocumentId': 'fadb8718-bb7a-4349-b22f-4fdc83051340',\\n    'publish': True\\n}\\n\\nres = requests.post(f'{BASE_URL}/api/documents.create', headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {TOKEN}'}, json=payload, verify=False)\\ndata = res.json()\\nprint('Status:', res.status_code, 'OK:', data.get('ok'))\\nif data.get('data'):\\n    doc_id = data['data']['id']\\n    print('Created doc id:', doc_id, 'url:', data['data']['url'])\\n    # clean up immediately\\n    del_res = requests.post(f'{BASE_URL}/api/documents.delete', headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {TOKEN}'}, json={'id': doc_id}, verify=False)\\n    print('Cleaned up test doc:', del_res.json())\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing document creation with parent in Outline\"","toolSummary":"\"Test document creation with parent\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
